.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH ngx-rm 1  "ngx-rm " 
.SH NAME
ngx\-rm \- Remove a site\*(Aqs configuration (a backup is kept)
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBngx\-rm\fR [\fB\-\-delete\-cert\fR] [\fB\-y\fR|\fB\-\-yes\fR] [\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fISITE\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Remove a site\*(Aqs configuration (a backup is kept)
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-delete\-cert\fR
Also delete its certbot certificate (`certbot delete`)
.TP
\fB\-y\fR, \fB\-\-yes\fR
Don\*(Aqt ask for confirmation
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Show what would change without touching anything
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fISITE\fR>
Site ID (from `ngx ls`) or any of its domain names
.SH EXTRA
Examples:
  sudo ngx rm 5
  sudo ngx rm old.example.com \-\-delete\-cert \-y
